      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BELIEVE IN BETTOR (3) after having placed second in two of his three previous runs scored a well deserved win at his latest appearance over 2185m at Pinjarra, scoring by 6 metres as the favourite after being on the pace throughout. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Tackles a similar assignment and he can go right on with the job. BROOME BEACH (6) was yet again about the mark last time out when runner-up over 2185m at Pinjarra, beaten 7 metres. Won't find this any harder and he can go one better without surprising. SWEETER THE BETTOR (7) was responsible for a better effort last time out when third over 2130m at Gloucester Park. Should run a big race. WAY OF THE WORLD (9) is open to further improvement at his third run back from a spell after getting home last time out over 2242m at Narrogin.",
